 "sentences": [
  "At 10:59 on 11 November 1918, one minute before the war ended, an American soldier charged a machine gun.",
  "The armistice was signed around five that morning, but took effect at eleven.",
  "Henry Gunther, 23, was a bank worker from Baltimore.",
  "A censored letter home had cost him his sergeant's stripes.",
  "Near a French village, he charged a German roadblock and was shot dead.",
  "Pershing's command named him the last American killed in the war.",
  "Other nations lost men that morning too.",
